    "result_text": "Done. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a computed `ownerSegment` field (`<TIER>_<AREA>`) exposed on the owner response.\n\n**Three files touched, each change small and isolated:**\n\n1. **`OwnerSegment.java`** (new) \u2014 a self-contained helper with a single static method. TIER is `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel >= 3` else `STANDARD`; AREA is `METRO` when `Locality.locality(owner)` is `NSW`/`VIC`/`QLD` else `REGIONAL`. Zero surrounding complexity, mirrors the existing `Locality`/`MembershipLevel` helper style.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one `@Mapping` line delegating to `OwnerSegment.of(membershipLevel(owner), owner)`, reusing the mapper's existing `membershipLevel(owner)` computation rather than duplicating it. No existing method was modified.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 one read-only `ownerSegment` schema property so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nThe two new acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known Sydney/NSW owner, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for a random-city owner) pass, and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nI kept structural impact low by not growing any existing method: the segment logic lives in a brand-new class with `WMC_other = 0`, and the only edit to a complex class (`OwnerMapper`) is a single annotation line delegating outward.",
